  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88201f4f4f3247558c87e55aa4fb8ac4, type: 3}
  m_Name: EileenFirst
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: HiddenHarbours.World::HiddenHarbours.World.DialogueDef
  Id: dialogue.eileen_first
  FirstLines:
  - 'Eileen Doiron. I keep the school — one room, and lately not a great many in it.'
  - 'Eleven children when I started here. Four now. The rest went up the road, and the
    road doesn''t send them back.'
  - 'So I teach mine what the road can''t: the tide table, the compass, and how to keep
    their own accounts. You came the other way, which makes you rare. Don''t waste it.'
  RepeatLines:
  - 'Still here. Still four of them. Read your tide before you cross that bar.'
